Fillets: the corner of a blend rolling on an edge and a blend whose
contact lies on the face the first one consumes (mitcad#1500).

The roof slab's eave rounded with 0.9 or 1 (1650): the tip's blend rolls
on the eave's obtuse edge and consumes the eave. The eave's end edge (90
degrees, between the eave and the end face), rounded too, has its contact
on the eave all along, inside the consumed face; at the tip's vertex the
two stripes have no common face. The corner went to PerformMoreThreeCorner,
which put the tip's blend's ends off the solid; the topology then failed
(TopoDS_FrozenShape, or a crash in TopOpeBRepBuild).

The two blends meet first where the end edge's contact on the eave reaches
the obtuse edge, at its other end: from there their intersection runs up
to the end face, the end edge's blend is cut down to a triangle at the
obtuse edge's end (between that intersection, its contact on the end face
and its cut by the underside), and the tip's blend runs on the obtuse edge
from that point.

- ChFi3d_IsInFront: where the two SurfData have no common face, a side of
  one on curve E (rolling on E) and the other's contact on a face of E
  whose end away from the vertex lies on E: that face is their common
  face, the parameters those of that end's point on both (projected on the
  rolling side's line).
- PerformTwoCornerbyInter: the big stripe's point on the pivot is taken on
  its contact by projection where its parameter there is off the point
  (the rolling blend's SurfData runs on past the spine's end, 0011).
- Compute, after the corners: a contact of a stripe of one SurfData that
  the corner at one end cut down to its point on an arc at the other end
  is one point: the corner's point index is replaced by the one on the arc
  (in the stripes and the corner's curves), its parameter the other end's;
  a rolling side that starts there gets that point on the arc, and its
  obstacle edge goes whole (no point there, cut at its vertex beyond, as
  at a rolling blend's end at a vertex).
- ChFi3d_FilDS: such a side of a stripe of one SurfData gives a
  degenerated edge of the blend's face, no curve on its face.
- ChFi3d_CutConsumedFaces: an end of the rolling blend short of the
  obstacle's vertex, where another stripe's contact on the consumed face
  is reduced to that point, counts as an end at the nearer vertex, so that
  the consumed face goes.

